{"from": "claim:mt-18-18-binding-loosing", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-16-19-binding-loosing", "note": "The bind/loose authority of Matt 18:18 is spoken to the whole community, repeating Matt 16:19 to Peter (ch 16); see the ch 16 claim for its evidence."}
{"from": "text:community-rule-5-24-6-1", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mt-18-15-16-reproof-steps", "grade": "B", "note": "1QS 5.24-6.1 (Burrows 1956): members 'reprove his neighbor in truth and humility and loyal love', never in anger, and 'a man shall not bring against his neighbor a word before the masters without having rebuked him before witnesses' - the rebuke-before-witnesses step of the same procedure CD 9 records. 1QS itself has no alone-first step; Matthew's alone-then-witnesses sequence is the stricter start."}
{"from": "text:community-rule-5-24-6-1", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mt-18-17-tell-the-assembly", "grade": "C", "note": "The accusation 'before the masters' (the community's overseers) is where a reproof case ends up at Qumran, as CD 9 ends at 'the judges of the congregation' - communal authority as the escalation's endpoint, contextual for the ekklēsia step."}
